    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{21}{28}=\\frac34$, so she got the same fraction correct on both tests.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{21}{28}&=\\frac{21\\div7}{28\\div7}\\\\&=\\frac34\\end{align*}$$\nThe fractions are equivalent, so she performed the same on both tests. Comparing only the numerators does not compare the fractions.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
